***MUST READ***

This is a custom texture for the Milky Way, originally derived from Nick Risinger’s Milky Way panorama from the Photoscopic Sky Survey.
This image won the APOD (Astronomy Picture of the Day) award on May 20, 2011. It is protected by a non-commercial license (CC-BY-NC), 
so it MAY ONLY be used for non-commercial purposes, such as educational use.

For the textures in the “ha-enhanced” folder, I used Finkbeiner’s all-sky H-alpha emission survey
(a fairly popular survey for mapping the entire distribution of hydrogen-alpha emission gas across the celestial sphere) and applied
a blending technique in GIMP. And once again, these are not for commercial use.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Installation instructions:

Download the PNG image (milkyway.png) that I’ve included in each folder. I’ve organized the folders by number to avoid file name conflicts.
Then, place the milkyway.png file in your Stellarium installation directory, depending on where you’ve set that directory—for example:

D:\Stellarium\textures (I’ve placed it on drive D for this example)

Paste it there; this will overwrite Stellarium’s default Milky Way texture.
Restart Stellarium. The default Milky Way texture will now be replaced with the custom texture.
